I open the door to the café.
Inside, it is wonderfully warm.
The air smells of fresh coffee.
I hear quiet music.
The café is very full.
Many people are sitting at the tables.
They are drinking and talking.
I look for a free table.
I look around briefly.
Over there is a small table.
It stands by a large window.
I go over there quickly.
I take off my heavy winter coat.
I lay the coat on the wooden chair.
The coat reserves my spot.
But I keep my backpack.
The backpack stays safely on my shoulder.
Now I go to the counter.
